    id: "25ae17bf-8127-4b49-9281-e3c0b991c249",
    slug: "claret-cobbler",
    name: "Claret Cobbler",
    description: "A Claret Cobbler appears in Jerry Thomas' 1862 The Bart-enders' Guide . Sherry Cobbler. (Use large bar glass.) 2 wine-glasses of sherry. 1 table-spoonful of sugar. 2 0r 3 slices of orange. Fill a tumbler with shaved ice, shake well, and ornament with berries in season. Place a straw as represented in the wood-cut. Catawba Cobbler. (Use large bar glass.) 1 teaspoonful of sugar dissolved in one table-spoonful of water. 2 wineglasses of wine. Fill tumbler with shaved ice, and ornament with sliced orange and berries in season. Place a straw as described in the sherry cobbler. Claret Cobbler. (Use large bar glass.) This drink is made the same way as the Catawba cobbler, using claret wine instead of Catawba. Jerry Thomas, The Bart-enders' Guide, 1862 See: Cobblers cocktail history More",
