    id: "acb79db8-c621-4868-8b25-c2cb0e5b951f",
    slug: "jack-rose-cocktail",
    name: "Jack Rose Cocktail",
    description: "The first known Jack Rose recipe appears in Jacob Abraham Grohusko's 1908 Jack's Manual with the following recipe: \"1 teaspoon sugar 10 dashes Raspberry syrup 10 dashes lemon juice 5 dashes orange juice Juice \u00bd lime 75% cider brandy Fill glass with cracked ice, shake and strain, fill with fizz water and serve. By the time the Jack Rose reappears in Jacques Straub's 1914 Drinks it was reduced to just three ingredients, much closer to modern-day renditions: \"1 jigger Applejack. \u00bd lime \u00bc jigger grenadine syrup. Shake well.\" Like many great classics, this drink is served with numerous plausible origins for its name but given the 1908 appearance above, some are easily discounted: 1. The Jack Rose is named after the Jacqueminot rose, which in turn takes its name from the French general,",
