    slug: "million-dollar-cocktail",
    name: "Million Dollar Cocktail",
    description: "Some say the Million Dollar Cocktail was created as early as 1894 by Louis Eppinger (the bartender credited for creating the Bamboo Cocktail ) at The Grand Hotel, Yokohama, Japan. Others maintain it was created around 1910 by Ngiam Tong Boon at The Long Bar , Raffles Hotel, Singapore. While, in his 1939 book The Gentleman's Companion volume II , Charles H. Baker, Jr. credits his first recipe for a Million Dollar Cocktail to Shideaki Saito, \"Saito, No. 1 Bar Boy at The Imperial Hotel, Tokyo, Japan, 1926 , 1931 & 1932\", as his second recipe to \"Nomura the No. 1 Bar Boy at Tor Hotel, Kobe, dating from 1926, to 1931 & 1932.\" David Wondrich , the noted cocktail historian, discounts Singapore, Yokohama and Tokyo in favour of the Million Dollar Cocktail originating at the Shanghai Club i",
